WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:05.067
-From Studio 6B
in Rockefeller Center

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.701
in the heart of New York City,

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:09.467
it's "The Tonight Show
Starring Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.934
♪♪

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.300
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.901
-Tonight,
join Jimmy and his guests --

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.567
Kit Harington...
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:16.934
-...Tyler James Williams...

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.234
and featuring

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:21.501
Paul Shaffer and
the World's Most Dangerous Band.

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:23.968
♪♪

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:27.133
-Hey, am I in the right studio?
[ Finale plays ]

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:30.167
-And now here he is...
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:33.000
-...Jimmy Fallon!
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.100
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:39.501
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.667
-Let them know now!
-♪ Hey, hey, hey ♪

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:50.934
-Oh, man!
-♪ Heeeeey ♪

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:52.501
[ Music ends ]
-Paul! Come on!

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes! Yes!

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:57.234
That's exactly what
I'm talking about, right there.

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:58.834
Come on, now!

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:00.901
Oh, yes!

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:03.801
♪♪

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:07.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
Whoo! What a night!

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.601
Paul Shaffer, right there,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:11.767
Welcome the Most Dangerous Band.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:13.267
-Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.667
-Enjoy yourselves.
Welcome, everybody.

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.934
Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
You're here.

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:21.968
This is "The Tonight Show."

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.801
Be honest --
how many of you were clapping

00:01:23.801 --> 00:01:25.467
just to get the feeling
back in your hands?

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.834
[ Laughs ] This weekend,
the Northeast could be hit

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:31.834
with the coldest weather
in decades,

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:34.467
with temperatures dropping
as low as minus 40 degrees.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.300
[ Audience ohhs ]
Yeah.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.901
It is so cold that
President Biden's

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:39.968
burning classified documents
just to stay warm.

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:41.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:45.033
♪♪

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.234
It is so cold, Tom Brady
came out of retirement

00:01:47.234 --> 00:01:48.334
just to huddle with the guys.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.567
You know what I mean?

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.467
♪♪

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:53.968
It is so cold,
everyone looks like

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:56.234
they're in "Avatar" -- everyone.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:58.801
♪♪

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.367
It is --

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:03.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:04.868
There's a few more of these.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.501
It is so cold, even

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:09.133
Prince William and Harry's
relationship feels warm.

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:10.367
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:14.834
♪♪

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:18.801
I think
there's two or three more.

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.334
-Oh, what?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:22.834
-It is so -- Do you understand
how cold it is?

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:25.167
-How cold is it?

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:27.801
-It is so cold,
on Spirit Airlines,

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:30.100
they made all the passengers
roll up their window.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.133
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:32.334
♪♪

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:33.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:35.167
I mean,
it is freezing out there.

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.434
-I didn't understand that
till now.

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:38.167
-It is so cold,
the Empire State Building

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:40.067
is six inches shorter
than normal.

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:41.567
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:43.267
♪♪

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:44.934
[ Applause ]

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:46.100
This is the final one
right here.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.167
-All right.
-It is so cold --

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:50.467
It is so cold...

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:52.334
-How cold is it?
-How cold is it?

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:55.300
-It is so cold, George Santos
claimed it was hot.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.534
That's...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.534 --> 00:03:00.133
♪♪

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:01.400
[ Clicks tongue ]

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.767
Thanks.

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:08.834
Meanwhile, a reporter
in New Jersey

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:11.067
was asking people how they are
dealing with the cold weather,

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:12.400
and one guy had a pretty
unexpected response.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.834
Watch this.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.767
-This weekend, the cold --
how are you going to handle it?

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.367
What's the plan?
-I don't know.

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:19.968
I work in a freezer, so it's not
that big of a deal for me.

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:22.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:27.434
[ Laughter continues ]

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:29.300
-Looks more like
he's been locked in a freezer.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.601
Yeah, it's like, hey...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:34.000
In New Jersey,
he's working in a freezer.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.467
That sounds like something
the mob would say.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.501
"Vinny?
Oh, let's just say he's, uh,

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.767
[sniffs]
working in a freezer."

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:41.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:43.000
Well, guys,
everyone's talking about this.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.834
U.S. officials spotted
what they say

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:49.601
is a massive Chinese spy balloon
flying over Montana.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:51.400
Yeah, the spying is scary,

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.300
but the balloon part
makes it kind of cute.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.534
Right?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.734
It's like Putin saying,

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:58.467
"I'm hiding in my
underground bouncy house."

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:02.133
That's right --
officials said the balloon

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.400
was recently spotted
flying over Montana.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.934
Well, let's check in
on the balloon right now.

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:07.367
Let me see.
[ Wind rushing ]

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:10.100
Oh, that's the spy balloon
there.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.968
Oh, hey, wait, oh.

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:14.934
[ Wind rushing ]

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:16.033
[ Gunshot ]

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.534
There you go -- he took...

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:19.267
That's it right there.
"Yellowstone."

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:20.501
He takes care of it.

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:24.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.300
Well, switching gears,
some entertainment news --

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.100
this Sunday is
the 65th annual Grammy Awards.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.968
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:36.434
-65 years.
The Grammys are so old,

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:39.234
they're starting to not know
the performers at the Grammys.

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:42.033
[ Laughter ]
"Who's Bad Bunny?"

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:43.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:47.467
You can watch the Grammys
on CBS and Paramount+.

00:04:47.467 --> 00:04:49.801
In other words, you'll be
watching the Grammys on CBS.

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.300
[ Laughter ]
Did you guys see this?

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:55.067
Tickets to Beyoncé's tour
go on sale Monday.

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:56.200
And Ticketmaster said

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.300
that demand is already 800%

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.234
higher than what's available.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.534
Today, the Ticketmaster CEO
showed up to congress like,

00:05:03.534 --> 00:05:04.901
"Let's just get these hearings
out of the way.

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:06.634
Let's just do it."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:07.868
It'll be fun on Monday

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:09.300
when the CEO's
rocking back and forth

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.434
and mumbling,
"You just broke my soul.

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.367
You just broke my soul."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:15.501
Well, get this --
Amazon said that some customers

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:19.200
are now able to get their
delivery orders within hours.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.767
Yeah, it's crazy.

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:21.934
Now when you drunk-order stuff,

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:23.834
it shows up,
you're still drunk.

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:25.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.601
"Cool, I wanted this."

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:30.467
[ Laughter ]
"Finally."

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:32.868
And finally,
a new $10 million sculpture

00:05:32.868 --> 00:05:35.167
was just unveiled
in New York City.

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:38.100
Take a look at this thing.
Yeah, I don't know.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.734
It doesn't look like
a work of art.

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:42.667
It looks like a Chinese spy
balloon going into Starbucks.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.534
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show tonight.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:45.801
Give it up for

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:49.033
for Paul Shaffer and
the World's Most Dangerous Band!

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:50.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:58.000
♪♪

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.501
[ Music ends ]
Come on, now!

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:01.601
Come on.
-And you know that.

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:03.400
-Come on, now.
-Come on.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.267
-That's what I'm talking about.
Paul Shaffer, right there.

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:06.534
-Thank you, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:08.901
The World's Most Dangerous Band.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.133
-What a trip.

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:13.801
This is surreal to be here
after all this time.

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:17.701
-I'm so excited that you're here
and thankful that you're here.

00:06:17.701 --> 00:06:19.834
But this is --
when was the first time?

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:21.567
This has been -- What?
-Well, you know,

00:06:21.567 --> 00:06:23.200
this is such a coincidence
that we're here tonight,

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.033
because 41 years ago,
this very week,

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:29.901
was when David Letterman
came on the air right here,

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:30.968
right across the hall
here at NBC --

00:06:30.968 --> 00:06:32.234
-Is that right?

00:06:32.234 --> 00:06:33.601
-...with "The Late Show
with David Letterman."

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:34.801
-Oh, my gosh.
-So, this is, like,

00:06:34.801 --> 00:06:38.200
our 41st anniversary
that we're celebrating.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:42.200
And thanks to you,
I have reunited the entire band

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.968
from "The Letterman Show."
We're all here.

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:44.901
-Yes! That's what
I'm talking about.

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:46.200
Come on!
-All the favorites...

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-...boys and girl.

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:52.267
And we're just having the time
of our lives, thanks to you.

00:06:52.267 --> 00:06:56.133
-When -- When he -- When
David Letterman first started,

00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:57.634
he started
as a morning show, right?

00:06:57.634 --> 00:06:58.868
-That's right, yes, yes.

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:00.534
-And he asked you
to be the musical director?

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:02.167
-I got the call from him to do
"The Morning Show."

00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:03.767
It was right after
"Saturday Night --"

00:07:03.767 --> 00:07:05.667
I had done the first
five seasons

00:07:05.667 --> 00:07:07.133
of "Saturday Night Live"...
-That's right.

00:07:07.133 --> 00:07:09.200
-...as a pianist and a little
bit of performing and writing.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.901
-Yeah.
-And then, right, I got a call.

00:07:10.901 --> 00:07:13.501
"David Letterman is going
on the air

00:07:13.501 --> 00:07:15.334
at 10:00 in the morning, live."

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.534
And I -- I turned it down.
I turned him down.

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:18.767
-You turned it down?
-I did.

00:07:18.767 --> 00:07:20.434
-Why? Why?
-Couldn't get up that early.

00:07:20.434 --> 00:07:22.267
[ Laughter ]
But no --

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:24.467
-Why yeah, of course.
-It just didn't seem --

00:07:24.467 --> 00:07:26.267
I don't know, you know?
But luckily for me,

00:07:26.267 --> 00:07:29.801
when that show didn't happen,
they gave him another shot.

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:32.067
They gave him "The Late Show,"
the 12:30 spot.

00:07:32.067 --> 00:07:34.267
-Yeah.
And they called me again.

00:07:34.267 --> 00:07:36.868
And this time, I had
the sense enough to say yes.

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:39.601
And, you know,
here we are, 33 years later,

00:07:39.601 --> 00:07:41.133
between the two networks.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:41.133 --> 00:07:43.767
-We were all together.
Yeah.

00:07:43.767 --> 00:07:47.100
-You know what's --
I would have thought --

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.968
I thought about you,
and I was so happy.

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.734
But when I used to do
"Letterman" --

00:07:50.734 --> 00:07:52.601
First of all, I was a big fan.
I watched his show.

00:07:52.601 --> 00:07:54.767
I watched "Late Night"
all the time.

00:07:54.767 --> 00:07:57.667
And I love David Letterman --
he's a genius, so funny.

00:07:57.667 --> 00:07:58.968
But I remember,
when I did the show,

00:07:58.968 --> 00:08:01.734
I would be nervous to meet you.
-Ah!

00:08:01.734 --> 00:08:03.868
-Because, yeah.
I mean, I'm such a fan.

00:08:03.868 --> 00:08:05.634
And I was, like,
so nervous to be around you

00:08:05.634 --> 00:08:06.901
and meet you guys and watch you.

00:08:06.901 --> 00:08:09.567
But you not only changed
the game and raised the bar

00:08:09.567 --> 00:08:11.701
of what a band
can do on the show --

00:08:11.701 --> 00:08:12.834
obviously, Doc Severinsen --

00:08:12.834 --> 00:08:14.300
but then, you showed us
how to do --

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.901
take it to a next level.

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:19.934
And then I think you changed
the face of comedy as well,

00:08:19.934 --> 00:08:24.033
if I may say, because you would
laugh at a joke when --

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:25.701
You told me backstage,
by the way,

00:08:25.701 --> 00:08:27.167
for the first two episodes,
they didn't turn your mic on.

00:08:27.167 --> 00:08:28.968
-Well, that's another story.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:28.968 --> 00:08:32.234
-But when they turned your mic
on and Dave told a joke,

00:08:32.234 --> 00:08:34.434
and sometimes the audience
wouldn't really laugh.

00:08:34.434 --> 00:08:38.334
But you would go, "Ah."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.334 --> 00:08:40.467
And that's when you knew
it was funny.

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:42.601
And comedy nerds around at home
are going,

00:08:42.601 --> 00:08:44.501
"He's right --
that was a funny joke,

00:08:44.501 --> 00:08:46.033
and the audience
just didn't get it yet."

00:08:46.033 --> 00:08:48.767
And you guys went, "Ah."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:48.767 --> 00:08:50.968
-I didn't know I had
that much responsibility,

00:08:50.968 --> 00:08:52.167
but I'm thrilled to hear it,
though.

00:08:52.167 --> 00:08:54.267
-No. Now, I think,
because of you,

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:55.868
comedians everywhere,

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:57.968
comedians I know,
they all laugh like you.

00:08:57.968 --> 00:09:00.133
-Oh, is that right?
-Every comedian --

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:02.100
Tina Fey laughs like you.
-Ah.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.801
-You see a funny joke,
you go, "Ah."

00:09:03.801 --> 00:09:05.267
-Ah.
-That's you.

00:09:05.267 --> 00:09:06.701
-Ah. Ah.
-They're doing you.

00:09:06.701 --> 00:09:08.200
That's Paul Shaffer right there,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:10.868
I'm honored -- honored!
-I am humbled.

00:09:10.868 --> 00:09:13.067
Jimmy, I am humbled. I can't --
-Be honor--

00:09:13.067 --> 00:09:14.300
Beyond honored that you're here.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.667
-Well, you know, remember,
I mean, all of us

00:09:16.667 --> 00:09:19.033
look to Johnny Carson
as our model.

00:09:19.033 --> 00:09:22.133
And he used to have
Doc Severinsen at band leader

00:09:22.133 --> 00:09:24.167
and Ed on the panel to talk to.

00:09:24.167 --> 00:09:27.400
And I used to say, "I'm
a combination of Doc and Ed."

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.901
In other words, I'm "Ded."

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:30.834
[ Laughter ]
Basically, I'm "Ded."

00:09:30.834 --> 00:09:33.033
-That's exactly right, yeah.
-But I'm alive tonight.

00:09:33.033 --> 00:09:36.467
-[ Laughs ] Come on.
I'm happy you're here, bud.

00:09:36.467 --> 00:09:37.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:09:37.634 --> 00:09:39.467
♪♪

00:09:39.467 --> 00:09:42.234
Well, what a show.

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:43.567
What a show
we have for you tonight.

00:09:43.567 --> 00:09:45.801
He stars in the new film
"Baby Ruby,"

00:09:45.801 --> 00:09:48.167
which is in theaters
and on demand now.

00:09:48.167 --> 00:09:50.234
Kit Harington is here tonight!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:50.234 --> 00:09:53.868
♪♪

00:09:53.868 --> 00:09:58.534
Plus, he just won a Golden Globe
for his role on the hit series

00:09:58.534 --> 00:10:01.400
"Abbott Elementary,"
which airs Wednesdays on ABC.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.133
Tyler James Williams is here
tonight, too!

00:10:04.133 --> 00:10:05.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:06.634
♪♪

00:10:06.634 --> 00:10:08.334
And it's -- And it's Friday.

00:10:08.334 --> 00:10:10.033
-Friday.
-Today's Friday,

00:10:10.033 --> 00:10:11.968
and that's usually when I catch
up with some personal stuff.

00:10:11.968 --> 00:10:13.901
I check my inbox.
I return some emails.

00:10:13.901 --> 00:10:15.901
And, of course,
send out thank-you notes.

00:10:15.901 --> 00:10:17.734
And I was just running...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:17.734 --> 00:10:19.434
...running a bit behind.

00:10:19.434 --> 00:10:21.100
So, I thought if you guys
wouldn't mind, can I write out

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.000
my weekly thank-you notes
right now for you guys?

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:24.734 --> 00:10:27.367
Paul -- Paul, could I get some
"thank-you note writing" music?

00:10:27.367 --> 00:10:29.000
-Yes, here it is, yeah.
[ Somber music plays ]

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:30.501 --> 00:10:33.968
♪♪

00:10:33.968 --> 00:10:35.167
-So somber.
-It's so fun.

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:36.901
-So somber.
-This is so fun --

00:10:36.901 --> 00:10:38.300
just seeing this
and hearing this.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:39.934
I'm having the greatest time
right now.

00:10:39.934 --> 00:10:41.467
[ Breathes sharply ]

00:10:41.467 --> 00:10:43.367
♪♪

00:10:43.367 --> 00:10:45.868
Thank you, Beyoncé Tour,

00:10:45.868 --> 00:10:49.234
for making my newest hobby
refreshing Ticketmaster.

00:10:49.234 --> 00:10:50.734
[ Applause ]

00:10:50.734 --> 00:10:52.601
♪♪

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.968
♪♪

00:10:58.968 --> 00:11:03.701
Thank you, cocktail sauce,
for being an overly elegant name

00:11:03.701 --> 00:11:05.734
for something that's 90% Heinz.

00:11:05.734 --> 00:11:07.667
[ Laughter and applause ]
It's like, "Cocktail sauce?"

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:10.968
-Ooh-la-la!
-[ Chuckles ]

00:11:10.968 --> 00:11:14.267
-Mmm! Catsup.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:11:14.267 --> 00:11:16.133
♪♪

00:11:16.133 --> 00:11:20.100
Thank you, massive Chinese
spy balloon over Montana.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:21.501
I can't wait to see you

00:11:21.501 --> 00:11:23.300
in this year's
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:24.801
That's going to be --
That's going to be --

00:11:24.801 --> 00:11:28.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Hey!

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.434
Whoa!

00:11:30.434 --> 00:11:33.567
[ Chuckles ]
-Coming down 5th Ave.

00:11:34.567 --> 00:11:36.868
♪♪

00:11:36.868 --> 00:11:39.167
Thank you, snow mobiles,

00:11:39.167 --> 00:11:41.501
for looking like
a Transformer planking.

00:11:41.501 --> 00:11:43.434
[ Applause ]

00:11:43.434 --> 00:11:46.267
♪♪

00:11:48.968 --> 00:11:50.868
♪♪

00:11:50.868 --> 00:11:56.400
Thank you, Netflix
cracking down on shared logins,

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:59.100
for severing our last tie
to our college roommate.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:00.467
[ Laughter and applause ]
That's it.

00:12:00.467 --> 00:12:01.901
Now we're done.

00:12:01.901 --> 00:12:03.400
Goodbye.
Out of my life.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:04.968
-Yeah.
Never going to see them again.

00:12:04.968 --> 00:12:06.334
-Out of my life.

00:12:06.334 --> 00:12:08.601
♪♪

00:12:09.234 --> 00:12:10.767
♪♪

00:12:10.767 --> 00:12:16.267
Thank you, puffy coats,
for giving me full-body abs.

00:12:16.267 --> 00:12:17.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:17.868 --> 00:12:19.534
I've got a 20-pack.

00:12:19.534 --> 00:12:20.534
♪♪

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.567
-I got a washing machine.
-I got a 25-pack.

00:12:23.567 --> 00:12:25.701
[ Laughter ]

00:12:25.701 --> 00:12:27.701
♪♪

00:12:27.701 --> 00:12:30.267
-Thank you, Paul Shaffer.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:30.267 --> 00:12:35.300
When people -- When people talk
about legends on late-night TV,

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:38.000
you're number one
on everyone's Top Ten List.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.000
There you have it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.767
Those were our thank-you notes.

00:12:40.767 --> 00:12:42.834
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody!

00:12:42.834 --> 00:12:44.434
Come on back!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:44.434 --> 00:12:49.501
♪♪

00:12:49.501 --> 00:12:50.767
-♪ 3,000 ♪

00:12:50.767 --> 00:12:55.133
♪♪

